  "steps": [
   "Heat the oven to 200°C (180°C fan) with a baking tray inside. Line the tin with the pastry, prick the base with a fork and chill while you make the filling.",
   "Melt the butter in the frying pan over a medium heat. Add the leeks, turnips, thyme and a pinch of the salt. Cover and cook for 12 to 15 minutes, stirring now and then, until the turnips are tender.",
   "Whisk the eggs, milk, crème fraîche, mustard, nutmeg, the rest of the salt and plenty of pepper in the bowl. Stir in most of the cheese.",
   "Spoon the vegetables into the pastry case, pour over the egg mix and scatter over the last of the cheese.",
   "Set the tin on the hot tray and bake for 35 to 40 minutes, until golden with just a slight wobble in the middle. Cool for 10 minutes before slicing."
